id: pm-slack-standup-8smy
title: Keep publish-attestation bindings within their shell scope
description: "The verifier lets assignments inside multiline substitutions, subshells, and uninvoked functions leak into later top-level publishes, allowing an unattested publish to borrow provenance. Model child scopes and regression-test every known bypass."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-30T16:27:47.562Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-30T16:32:38.587Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-30T16:32:37.915Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-30T16:32:37.915Z"
author: pi-agent
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T16:32:37.388Z",pi-agent,"Scoped the segmenter across command substitutions, subshells, and function bodies; nested newlines can no longer persist scalar bindings globally. Added conservative unset handling and explicit regressions for heredoc, discarded binding, continuation, subshell, uninvoked function, and all three multiline child scopes. Revert proof: removing the nested-segment persistence guard made the multiline-substitution assertion fail 0 !== 1; restoring it passed. Coverage gate passes with 255 tests."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  scripts/verify-release-publish-attestation.ts,project
  test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts,project
tests[2]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
  npm test,project,pi-agent,"2026-08-30T16:32:36.777Z",local_mutation,fix/refuse-unattested-publish-fallback
  npm run coverage,project,pi-agent,"2026-08-30T16:32:36.777Z",local_mutation,fix/refuse-unattested-publish-fallback
close_reason: Child-scope and discarded bindings no longer attest top-level publishes; all known bypass regressions and the coverage gate pass.
body: ""
